WEBVTT

00:45.086 --> 00:49.424
DOONA!

01:07.650 --> 01:09.527
Ah, you're so heavy!

01:16.785 --> 01:18.661
Muah!

01:39.099 --> 01:40.892
- Hell there.
- Hello.

01:40.975 --> 01:42.519
They're all so pretty.

01:42.602 --> 01:44.646
Please let me know
if you have any questions.

01:49.275 --> 01:50.151
That's pretty.

01:50.235 --> 01:51.152
- Is it?
- Mm-hmm.

01:51.236 --> 01:53.154
- We have a matching one for men.
- You do?

01:53.655 --> 01:54.864
Here you go.

01:54.948 --> 01:55.907
Give it a try.

01:56.950 --> 01:58.159
Does it fit?

01:59.244 --> 02:00.703
What do you think?

02:00.787 --> 02:02.580
- Ooh!
- Ooh! It's nice.

02:02.664 --> 02:03.998
It really is nice.

02:04.082 --> 02:06.292
- Wanna get these?
- Okay, let's get them.

02:53.214 --> 02:55.175
MOM

03:07.478 --> 03:08.688
Whoo!

03:09.189 --> 03:10.106
Whoo!

03:10.690 --> 03:11.774
MOM

03:11.858 --> 03:13.484
Oh, um…

03:43.806 --> 03:44.807
Okay.

03:45.683 --> 03:46.851
Well,

03:46.935 --> 03:50.104
then you should probably do
what the doctor says. Don't you think?

03:50.188 --> 03:52.565
So, hey, listen, Mom.
We need to make a decision really soon.

03:52.649 --> 03:54.651
Once we do,
they can schedule the operation for her.

03:55.568 --> 03:56.402
Okay then.

04:02.200 --> 04:04.494
MINSONG NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
DEPARTMENT OF CLOTHING

04:07.163 --> 04:09.332
COME PICK ME UP RIGHT NOW
I'M TOO DRUNK TO WALK

04:09.415 --> 04:11.876
Okay, I sent it.

04:12.961 --> 04:14.128
Oh, you know,

04:14.879 --> 04:17.423
it's gonna be embarrassing
if no one comes.

04:18.591 --> 04:20.218
Well, then it's not meant to be.

04:23.221 --> 04:27.267
- To her destiny! Woo-hoo!
- To destiny! Cheers!

04:41.489 --> 04:45.368
So I went to my fortune teller,
and she said today I'll be lucky in love.

04:45.451 --> 04:46.494
- Seriously? Awesome!
- Yup.

04:46.577 --> 04:48.579
- Can I hang out with you?
- Of course.

04:48.663 --> 04:49.664
Yes!

04:50.957 --> 04:53.167
Can you come right now
to pick me up?

04:53.251 --> 04:55.128
I'm too drunk to walk.

04:57.672 --> 05:00.508
Uh, um… hey, I… I gotta bounce, dude.

05:00.591 --> 05:01.426
Huh?

05:01.509 --> 05:02.927
It's just, I gotta go right away.

05:03.011 --> 05:04.220
- Hey, where you going?
- Huh?

05:04.304 --> 05:05.138
- I'm sorry.
- Don't go.

05:05.221 --> 05:07.056
- Let me go.
- I thought we were gonna hang out!

05:07.140 --> 05:08.766
Look, look…
Chill. I'll be back.

05:08.850 --> 05:10.310
- Hey!
- See you later!

05:10.393 --> 05:13.604
Useless jerks, all of them. Pssh.

05:15.148 --> 05:16.482
Ugh!

05:18.860 --> 05:20.820
Someone's here.

05:21.571 --> 05:22.697
Oh!

05:22.780 --> 05:24.991
Look, someone came.
Look over there. He's standing.

05:25.950 --> 05:27.076
Oh…

05:27.160 --> 05:28.786
What the fuck? She was right.

05:31.122 --> 05:32.040
Hey.

05:32.123 --> 05:34.459
Wake up, I-Ra. Hey. Come on. Wake up.

05:34.542 --> 05:36.002
Wake up. Wake up.

05:39.672 --> 05:40.840
Huh?

05:55.772 --> 05:59.650
- All right, we're home!
- Let go of my ears.

05:59.734 --> 06:02.528
We made it!

06:03.821 --> 06:04.655
I'm tired.

06:06.532 --> 06:09.118
Hey. No wait! Ah.

06:21.422 --> 06:23.383
When you look at me like that,

06:23.466 --> 06:24.967
it makes me wanna make out.

06:39.649 --> 06:41.484
Ugh, hey!

06:41.567 --> 06:44.445
Why'd you move so fast? Did you dodge me
'cause you don't know how to kiss?

06:44.529 --> 06:47.990
- It's 'cause you're drunk.
- Well, thanks to you, not anymore!

06:48.658 --> 06:51.119
- Well, are you sure?
- Yes, totally.

06:52.286 --> 06:53.162
Hmm?

06:58.793 --> 06:59.836
I like you too, I-ra.

07:01.170 --> 07:03.047
See? I'm not the only clueless one here.

07:07.677 --> 07:08.719
Wow.

07:10.847 --> 07:11.973
What now?

07:12.682 --> 07:14.475
He's so freaking hot.

07:47.091 --> 07:50.928
- Do you know how cute you are?
- Yes, you are very cute, aren't you?

07:51.012 --> 07:56.184
- His face is squishy like tofu, isn't it?
- Tofu, tofu, Won-taeky, tofu!

07:56.267 --> 07:57.477
- Stinky tofu!
- I know.

07:57.560 --> 08:00.354
- I love his jacket as well.
- It looks like stinky tofu!

08:00.438 --> 08:03.149
- It's Yun-taek, all right?
- You look like stinky tofu.

08:03.232 --> 08:04.609
- Taeky, Won-taeky!
- Won-taeky!

08:04.692 --> 08:05.860
- Let's have another!
- Okay.

08:05.943 --> 08:08.237
Your friend I-ra,
how come she's not here?

08:08.321 --> 08:10.448
- Toast!
- Let's drink to us, okay?

08:10.531 --> 08:13.034
- All right! Cheers!
- Cheers!

08:13.117 --> 08:14.994
- Mmm!
- Mmm!

08:15.077 --> 08:17.246
You drink like such a stud!

08:17.330 --> 08:19.874
- Wait, what's this? It's a dimple, right?
- That was really good.

08:19.957 --> 08:21.876
- He even has dimples!
- Ah!

08:21.959 --> 08:23.586
- So cute!
- Your dimples are so cute!

08:23.669 --> 08:25.963
- You're dressed so well today.
- I can't even believe it!

08:26.047 --> 08:28.424
- Let's do this thing right.
- Oh!

08:28.508 --> 08:31.177
- The stinky tofu is stripping for us!
- I'll pour this time.

08:31.260 --> 08:33.763
- Ah!
- That's great. That's great. Yeah!

08:33.846 --> 08:35.806
- Yeah! Let's go!
- Okay!

11:08.709 --> 11:10.127
Whoo!

11:10.961 --> 11:11.879
Whoo!

11:20.096 --> 11:22.223
- Yay!
- Whoo!

11:31.607 --> 11:33.901
It's so nice.

11:36.028 --> 11:38.781
Your taste in things is very predictable.
You know that?

11:40.449 --> 11:41.575
I know it is.

11:42.535 --> 11:44.537
I've always been this way.

11:45.913 --> 11:47.540
I like things that are ordinary.

11:48.040 --> 11:49.792
Well, you're not ordinary.

11:49.875 --> 11:50.751
Hmm.

12:06.475 --> 12:08.436
Do you ever wish
you could go back?

12:10.479 --> 12:12.231
- Hmm?
- You were a singer, hmm?

12:13.649 --> 12:16.318
I'm sure that you miss it
'cause it was your life at the time.

12:17.111 --> 12:18.446
You were born to perform, I think.

12:23.451 --> 12:24.493
Would you allow it?

12:26.287 --> 12:29.623
What kind of question is that?
If you want to perform, you should.

12:31.709 --> 12:33.461
I'd love to see you sing, you know?

12:35.921 --> 12:37.673
I would support you no matter what.

12:50.436 --> 12:52.480
I forget sometimes how naive you are.

12:58.486 --> 13:00.404
What if they say we can't be together?

13:01.322 --> 13:02.323
Then what?

13:04.617 --> 13:05.451
Uh…

13:13.209 --> 13:14.293
Hello?

13:14.376 --> 13:16.003
Your voice sounds scratchy.

13:17.296 --> 13:18.672
Are you feeling all right?

13:19.215 --> 13:20.508
I'm okay.

13:22.718 --> 13:24.637
I just got here,

13:24.720 --> 13:25.930
and I miss you already.

13:28.140 --> 13:29.225
So do I.

13:33.979 --> 13:35.689
Has it been raining there at all?

13:37.817 --> 13:38.734
No.

13:39.443 --> 13:41.070
It's overcast, but no rain yet.

13:50.538 --> 13:53.123
Apparently, this year,
we're supposed to get a lot of rain.

14:47.469 --> 14:49.805
I SAW MY LOVE DOONA
AT THE NERD CONNECTION CONCERT

14:49.889 --> 14:51.265
DOONA THE GODDESS! BEAUTIFUL!

14:51.348 --> 14:54.643
Lee Doona!
Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

14:54.727 --> 14:56.687
LEE DOONA MADE A SURPRISE APPEARANCE

14:56.770 --> 14:59.315
Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

15:33.557 --> 15:35.768
LAWSUIT NOTICE FOR DAMAGE CLAIM
FROM BREACH OF CONTRACT

15:35.851 --> 15:37.102
Hello.

15:37.186 --> 15:40.773
I'm Jung Ji-guk, the legal representative
of MSA Entertainment.

15:41.398 --> 15:44.401
My client has commenced proceedings
against you for financial damages

15:44.485 --> 15:47.112
arising from the breach
of your exclusive contract.

15:47.196 --> 15:49.823
I believe you received
the notice via certified mail.

15:50.324 --> 15:53.452
Moving forward, I'd prefer
to liaise with your legal representative

15:53.535 --> 15:54.495
rather than yourself.

16:38.288 --> 16:41.792
LAWSUIT NOTICE FOR DAMAGE CLAIM
FROM BREACH OF CONTRACT

16:41.875 --> 16:45.254
YOU HAVE INCURRED A PENALTY
DUE TO YOUR UNILATERAL BREACH OF CONTRACT

16:57.933 --> 16:59.268
Don't smoke in here.

17:07.943 --> 17:09.653
Did you really
have to take things this far?

17:13.032 --> 17:14.658
You think this is all my doing?

17:21.206 --> 17:22.624
I would've taken things farther.

17:22.708 --> 17:25.210
As I recall, we agreed
to terminate the contract

17:25.294 --> 17:27.755
on the condition
I wouldn't sign elsewhere.

17:32.509 --> 17:34.428
Did you really think that was possible?

17:35.179 --> 17:36.680
I may have washed my hands of you,

17:37.806 --> 17:39.641
but it won't be as easy with President Ma.

17:42.102 --> 17:44.063
You set a bad precedent in this industry.

17:44.146 --> 17:46.607
They're not letting someone like you
off the hook like that.

17:50.277 --> 17:51.779
So what happens next?

17:51.862 --> 17:54.990
Regardless of the compensation,
they'll make this trial drag on endlessly,

17:55.074 --> 17:56.992
because it's their way of torturing you,

17:57.076 --> 17:59.036
all the while,
destroying your public image

17:59.119 --> 18:01.955
with a smear campaign
with no regard for the truth.

18:02.039 --> 18:03.665
How will you make a comeback then?

18:05.084 --> 18:06.585
Your career will be completely over.

18:19.431 --> 18:21.350
So just say what I should do, then.

18:21.934 --> 18:23.143
You should already know.

18:23.894 --> 18:25.437
This'll be your last chance, you got it?

18:26.355 --> 18:28.649
I've taken care of the videos
posted online.

18:28.732 --> 18:31.527
Now, it's time for you
to get rid of that guy.

18:32.111 --> 18:33.153
If you make a comeback,

18:33.237 --> 18:35.489
he'll be the first thing
they'll rip to shreds.

18:40.536 --> 18:43.205
- Hey, you get everything?
- Of course. I got it all.

18:43.288 --> 18:44.123
Oh, good, I do too.

18:44.206 --> 18:46.333
- We have enough?
- Yeah, dude, for sure.

18:46.416 --> 18:48.335
- Do you have your keys?
- Yeah, left pocket.

18:48.877 --> 18:50.045
Hmm…

18:50.546 --> 18:51.463
Got it.

18:55.425 --> 18:57.636
Hey, what are you wearing?
Is that a ring?

18:57.719 --> 18:59.138
Did you get a girlfriend?

18:59.221 --> 19:00.472
You finally noticed.

19:00.556 --> 19:01.890
You should've told me!

19:01.974 --> 19:03.600
- Well, is she hot?
- Very.

19:03.684 --> 19:05.185
What the hell, man?

19:05.269 --> 19:07.229
- I wanna meet her.
- All right, you will.

19:07.312 --> 19:10.023
You gotta tell me
how I can meet a pretty girl too.

19:15.279 --> 19:17.197
Won-yeong
is being discharged on Sunday.

19:17.281 --> 19:20.200
I'll deal with that and come up
right after, even if it's late.

19:20.784 --> 19:22.077
Okay, gotta go, Doona.

19:23.203 --> 19:24.663
Okay, bye.

19:24.746 --> 19:25.747
I'll call you.

19:42.181 --> 19:44.099
I'm off to Na-yeong's. I'll see you later!

19:44.183 --> 19:45.934
Oh! Here. Take this.

19:47.269 --> 19:48.312
It's from Doona.

19:49.479 --> 19:50.606
Thanks so much, Doona.

19:51.815 --> 19:53.317
- See you.
- Bye.

19:58.530 --> 20:01.408
You didn't need to bring gifts, seriously.

20:01.491 --> 20:03.243
I heard you're taking time off.

20:03.327 --> 20:04.286
Yeah.

20:04.369 --> 20:07.289
My father used to pay
for my tuition fees, so I'm broke.

20:07.789 --> 20:11.293
Besides, it's hard to see
you and Won-jun together, so I need space.

20:11.835 --> 20:14.046
You don't have to be
quite so honest, you know.

20:15.547 --> 20:17.799
Oh, I got a new job,
so next meal's my treat.

20:20.385 --> 20:22.763
So I guess this must mean
that you don't hate me that much?

20:23.847 --> 20:25.015
Hmm…

20:25.849 --> 20:27.392
How could I possibly hate you?

20:27.893 --> 20:30.729
My father has run for office
three separate times and always lost.

20:31.438 --> 20:34.233
And every time he loses,
he'll talk trash about the winner.

20:34.733 --> 20:35.692
Honestly, though,

20:36.318 --> 20:39.238
is it really the winner’s fault
for winning?

20:39.321 --> 20:40.989
Blaming the winner when you lose

20:41.073 --> 20:44.534
is really only going to make you
look a lot more pathetic. It's a bad look.

20:47.663 --> 20:49.039
If I'm being honest,

20:49.581 --> 20:51.166
your dad is totally a jerk.

20:53.752 --> 20:55.087
I talked with him once.

20:56.338 --> 20:58.131
It was the night
you passed out at my house.

20:59.341 --> 21:02.135
- Um, yes, hello?
- You crazy bitch.

21:02.219 --> 21:05.264
What kind of lowlifes are you out with
at this time of night?

21:06.932 --> 21:08.642
Ugh! No way!

21:09.768 --> 21:11.186
I had no idea.

21:13.855 --> 21:14.773
Oh.

21:14.856 --> 21:17.901
That's when I started
to really feel for you.

21:18.902 --> 21:22.489
I felt awful you were trying so hard
to appear like nothing was wrong.

21:24.908 --> 21:26.743
Ugh, this is super embarrassing.

21:26.827 --> 21:29.329
Don't feel embarrassed.
Friends don't judge.

21:29.413 --> 21:31.039
I've been living life all wrong.

21:31.707 --> 21:33.917
Ignoring my problems
doesn't solve anything.

21:34.001 --> 21:34.918
Mm-mm.

21:36.169 --> 21:38.755
Plenty of people
are living their lives wrong.

21:38.839 --> 21:39.840
You're not one of them.

21:40.424 --> 21:41.258
Hmm.

21:46.680 --> 21:48.098
So what brought you here, Doona?

21:51.393 --> 21:52.352
I just missed you.

21:54.313 --> 21:55.981
You're a friend. I told you that.

24:30.385 --> 24:34.639
NOWDROWZ
INSOMNIA, NON-HABIT-FORMING, SLEEP AID

25:18.558 --> 25:19.768
Oh, you're up.

25:20.352 --> 25:21.603
Want some coffee?

25:22.687 --> 25:23.605
Okay.

25:24.147 --> 25:25.482
I'll make the toast, then.

26:29.963 --> 26:32.465
Go ahead. Talk. I assume
there's something you want to say.

26:32.549 --> 26:35.343
I need you to stop…
whatever business you have with her.

26:37.345 --> 26:38.722
And leave her alone for good.

26:39.222 --> 26:40.974
And no more personal visits. You got that?

26:43.268 --> 26:45.020
Why are you so angry over all this?

26:45.895 --> 26:48.106
You're about 21, 22, right?

26:48.189 --> 26:49.649
Is your military service done yet?

26:50.233 --> 26:52.777
So by the time you finish university
and find a job

26:52.861 --> 26:55.989
and whatever else you might do,
that's at least five years more.

26:57.198 --> 26:59.075
Do you really plan on
dating her till then?

26:59.909 --> 27:01.703
- Realistically speaking--
- I certainly hope so.

27:04.914 --> 27:06.082
Okay, kid.

27:06.583 --> 27:08.043
I bet you're also the type

27:08.126 --> 27:10.879
to believe in things
like fairies and ghosts

27:10.962 --> 27:15.133
or past-life connections, right?
I guess it's easier when you're a kid.

27:15.216 --> 27:17.594
Then why don't you let us kids
figure it out ourselves?

27:17.677 --> 27:20.013
Too much is riding on this
for me to do that. Sorry, kid.

27:20.096 --> 27:22.265
Quit exaggerating.

27:26.269 --> 27:27.228
I wasn't exaggerating.

27:28.438 --> 27:30.732
All that really matters
is what the public thinks of her,

27:30.815 --> 27:33.985
and letting her come back
after how she acted is a big risk for us.

27:34.069 --> 27:36.529
Her current approval rating
has hit rock bottom.

27:36.613 --> 27:38.323
No one knows what to expect at all.

27:38.406 --> 27:40.533
If Doona alone
stood to make ten billion won,

27:40.617 --> 27:43.078
well then, I'm sure
we're risking ten times that.

27:43.161 --> 27:45.121
Given what's already at stake,
no one's dumb enough

27:45.205 --> 27:47.123
to add a boyfriend to the equation.
You got it?

27:47.207 --> 27:49.542
Not the label, not even Doona.

27:52.545 --> 27:54.047
So who should leave who alone?

27:54.839 --> 27:55.674
Take a guess.

29:18.590 --> 29:21.050
I think Doona
has had a lot to think about,

29:21.134 --> 29:22.927
and ultimately,
what she wants from the company

29:23.011 --> 29:26.222
is to give her a little bit more say
in all her future work.

29:26.723 --> 29:28.516
What do you think, President Ma?

29:28.600 --> 29:30.810
Oh, of course. She should have a say

29:30.894 --> 29:32.812
and make the kind of music
she really likes.

29:32.896 --> 29:33.855
So moving forward,

29:33.938 --> 29:35.774
the company will allow Doona
to be creative lead

29:35.857 --> 29:37.692
and take the music
any direction she wants?

29:37.776 --> 29:40.111
Yes. Why would we interfere, huh?

29:40.195 --> 29:41.696
She can make whatever.

29:41.780 --> 29:45.325
After all, she's the songwriter here,
and our job is to support her, right?

29:45.408 --> 29:48.495
Doona, moving forward,
please feel free to do what you want.

29:48.578 --> 29:50.413
You can make the music you like, hmm?

29:50.997 --> 29:53.666
How many tracks did you say
were already in the works?

29:54.167 --> 29:56.419
We have about five or six songs
featuring artists

29:56.503 --> 29:58.671
that Doona herself selected. Hmm.

30:01.549 --> 30:04.302
If there's anything you need right away,
ask Mr. Ko.

30:05.220 --> 30:07.639
I'll handle the move,
so you don't need to worry about it.

30:08.598 --> 30:11.142
But let me know if there's
anything you need from the house, okay?

30:13.228 --> 30:14.687
It's strange, isn't it?

30:15.814 --> 30:17.232
That I can sing again.

30:17.982 --> 30:19.567
I didn't think I'd be able to.

30:22.278 --> 30:24.113
How should I let him go?

30:25.365 --> 30:27.450
You're good at discarding people, right?

30:28.201 --> 30:29.452
So what should I do?

30:30.662 --> 30:31.579
Tell me how.

30:33.790 --> 30:35.917
How should I break Won-jun's heart, huh?

30:36.709 --> 30:38.920
Because I don't have it in me to do it.

30:42.757 --> 30:43.675
I'll sing

30:45.009 --> 30:48.555
and dance well enough to justify
the money that's been re-invested in this.

30:49.806 --> 30:52.308
More than enough
for them to forget their losses.

30:52.392 --> 30:55.395
And, you know, I'm not doing this
because of the lawsuit.

30:55.478 --> 30:58.439
- And it has nothing to do with you either.
- I know.

30:59.524 --> 31:03.194
I realized my happiness
is the most important thing. All right?

31:14.873 --> 31:15.957
I met your friend.

31:17.083 --> 31:19.460
He came to my office. He didn't tell you?

31:20.962 --> 31:23.756
From now on, cut contact
with everyone you know. Is that clear?

31:24.841 --> 31:27.135
Get some rest. Tomorrow's a busy day.

31:27.969 --> 31:29.429
What did you say to Won-jun?

31:35.518 --> 31:39.314
There wasn't really much to say.
Not big on entertaining kids.

32:03.880 --> 32:04.923
Thanks a lot, everybody.

32:05.006 --> 32:09.218
I gotta say, tonight's show has been
particularly nerve-racking for me,

32:09.302 --> 32:11.930
and the reason is that I spotted

32:12.013 --> 32:13.806
a familiar face in the audience

32:14.390 --> 32:15.767
earlier this evening.

32:15.850 --> 32:18.353
I mean, I'm a huge fan of hers.

32:18.436 --> 32:21.731
The one and only
Dream Sweet's Lee Doona is here.

32:24.776 --> 32:26.110
I'm right, aren't I?

32:27.904 --> 32:32.533
Could I invite you to…
maybe accompany me on stage tonight?

32:36.663 --> 32:39.457
Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

32:39.540 --> 32:43.878
Lee Doona! Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

32:43.962 --> 32:49.759
Lee Doona! Lee Doona!
Lee Doona! Lee Doona!

